{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Layer Matrix Computation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Layer Matrix Computation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"layer matrix computation layer matrix computation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Layer Matrix Computation.md","fileName":"Layer Matrix Computation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Layer Matrix Computation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 02:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Artificial Neural Network Structure]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Artificial Neural Network Structure","Activation Function","Feedforward Neural Computation","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Layer Matrix Computation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Layer Matrix Computation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"layer matrix computation layer matrix computation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Layer Matrix Computation.md","fileName":"Layer Matrix Computation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Layer Matrix Computation","heading":"Layer Matrix Computation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The weighted sums for a fully connected neural-network layer can be calculated together. Put the preceding layer's activations in a vector and the connection weights in a matrix; their product produces a vector of weighted sums for the next layer's neurons. An [[Activation Function]] is then applied element by element.\n\nThis is the matrix view of [[Feedforward Neural Computation]]. It replaces many separately described neuron calculations with one structured operation, while preserving the same connections. Kelleher uses the view to explain why matrix-oriented hardware can accelerate repeated forward and training passes through a network.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Artificial Neural Network Structure","